messages:
Maria: quick question — we're rolling out the payments service and need to decide how to wire the DB password into the pod. chart currently supports `env:` with `valueFrom.secretKeyRef` or inline `env` strings. which approach should we standardize on?
Sanjay: short answer: prefer secretKeyRef (k8s secret) for prod, but chart should support both for dev overrides.
Maria: ok. there's also a terraform change that will create the secret for prod (`kubernetes_secret`), but dev clusters often set plain values via CI. want to make sure helm templating won't explode.
Elaine: +1 on support both. recommend adding a small helper template in _helpers.tpl to pick `value` vs `valueFrom`.
Josh: example helper I use:
```yaml
{{- define "common.containerEnv" -}}
{{- $name := .name -}}
{{- $val := .value | default "" -}}
{{- $secret := .secretRef | default nil -}}
{{- if $val }}
- name: {{ $name }}
  value: "{{ $val }}"
{{- else if $secret }}
- name: {{ $name }}
  valueFrom:
    secretKeyRef:
      name: {{ $secret.name }}
      key: {{ $secret.key | default "password" }}
{{- else }}
# no env provided for {{ $name }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
```
Maria: nice. one more: our values.yaml currently has `db.password` and `db.secretRef.name`. if both are set, which should win?
Robin: enforce precedence: explicit `db.password` should only be allowed for local/dev. For clarity: if `db.password` present, render `value`; else if `db.secretRef.name` present, render `valueFrom`. Document this in chart README.
Sanjay: note: Helm's `tpl` can be handy if you allow env interpolation from other values, but avoid complex `tpl` usage for secrets. keep templates auditable.
Elaine: also, CI/CD needs to be updated: our terraform change will create the secret named `payments-db-<env>`. we should add a smoke step to the pipeline that checks secret exists before deploying helm. devops-bot: terraform apply finished for `payments-db-prod` in 2m 14s (plan ID: tf-9821).
Maria: that plan created the secret as a k8s Secret with `stringData`. good. Josh, can you add the helper and a small unit test (helm template output) to the chart?
Josh: yes, I'll add helper + a test that renders three cases: (1) value only, (2) secretRef only, (3) neither => error/warn. will open a PR.
Sanjay: tiny template tip: when rendering `valueFrom.secretKeyRef.name` use `{{ required "secretRef.name required" .Values.db.secretRef.name }}` in the test case for prod to fail early.
Maria: sounds good. also, doc the terraform secret naming convention in infra repo so teams know how to reference it in values.
Elaine: action items:
- Josh: add helper + tests + README snippet (PR by EOD)
- Robin: add pipeline check for secret existence (ticket created)
- Sanjay: update chart maintainers guide about `tpl` limits
- Maria: update payments deploy manifest to use secretRef in prod values override

Josh: pinging — I'll try to keep the helper minimal and clear. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/charts/pull/418 (draft)
Maria: thanks all. if anyone needs the terraform output or secret name: terraform module: infra/k8s-secrets/payments, secret name: `payments-db-prod`, key: `password`.
Sanjay: FYI you can verify with `kubectl get secret payments-db-prod -o yaml` or `kubectl get secret payments-db-prod -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 --decode`.
Robin: I'll attach the pipeline ticket: TCK-1248.
Elaine: closing loop — once PR merges we'll switch prod values to reference the secret and run the pipeline check in staging. :thumbsup:
Maria: perfect, thanks everyone.
